 "brief": "A 90 degree hose elbow in PETG (FDM, layers along Z) for shop air at 2 bar gauge. The bore is 12 mm: it comes in along X from x = -30 to the corner at the origin, then goes up along Z to z = 34. The inlet end has a flange on the plane x = -30 (y = -16 to 16, z = -16 to 16, 5 mm thick) bolted to a manifold with four M4 screws at y, z = +-11. The outlet is a 16 mm hose barb, the top 14 mm of the vertical leg. Keep the part inside x = -30 to 12, y = -16 to 16, z = -16 to 34. The hose can tug the barb sideways with 40 N in any direction. Safety factor 3 on the pressure, 2 on the tug.",
